{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Depart, etc.</b> Rabbi Moses the Kohen, of blessed memory, said: from within Babylon. But the correct view in my eyes is that the word סורו סורו (depart, depart), unclean, applies to the entire exile that is among the nations." "<b>Depart, depart.</b> Sometimes [the repetition] indicates haste, as in סורה אדוני (Judges 4:18)." "<b>Go out from there.</b> Each and every one from the place of his exile." "<b>Unclean, do not touch.</b> That they separate from the nations of the world." "<b>Go out from her midst.</b> Each one from the land of his exile, for in all the passages above there is no mention of Babylon." "<b>Purify.</b> Nif'al pattern, and it should have had a dagesh because of the doubling letter." "<b>Bearers of the vessels of YHWH.</b> They are Israel, bearers of the Torah. Some say it refers to the Levites, who are bearers of the Ark. The first is correct in my eyes."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:12.434243017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}